    "narrative": "Our primary offensive engine today is **Lawrence Butler** (73.41), who warrants an elite-tier start against Jared Jones. His score is bolstered by a potent combination of a 10% park factor bump and a favorable 13% platoon adjustment against the right-hander, making him our most reliable source of production. **Geraldo Perdomo** (61.72) and **Tyler Freeman** (60.46) follow closely; **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits from a soft matchup against Walbert Ure\u00f1a\u2019s 4.65 xERA and favorable park dimensions, while **Tyler Freeman** leverages an 8% boost from his lead-off/two-hole role and a helpful wind direction to offset the challenge of facing Shota Imanaga.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved our middle-of-the-pack starters, where **Bryson Stott** (59.49) narrowly squeezed into the lineup over **Gleyber Torres** (48.29). While **Gleyber Torres** carries a high-upside lead-off role, he suffers from a significant 13% dynamic platoon penalty against Kai-Wei Teng. In contrast, **Bryson Stott** is bolstered by an 88% stolen base allowance from opposing starter Ryan Gusto\u2014a critical factor given our league's scarcity of speed\u2014which provided the marginal edge needed to secure his spot. We remain thin at catcher and corner infield due to the unfortunate IL status of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Cal Raleigh**, **Will Smith**, and **Daulton Varsho**, forcing us to lean on depth pieces like **Jonathan Aranda** and **Gavin Sheets** to keep our daily efficiency above the threshold. \n\nMonitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, particularly **Masyn Winn**, whose current projection of 52.23 is highly sensitive to his slot in the order. If he slides down from the lead-off spot, his efficiency score will likely plummet, potentially forcing us to look toward bench reserves like **Luis Arraez** or **Matt Chapman** if they are confirmed in advantageous spots. We are also tracking the status of **Taylor Ward**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, and **Dylan Beavers** as potential high-leverage pivots should any weather or late lineup scratches materialize across the diamond.",
